Design of `classify_finding(stmt, finding)`:
```python
def parse_ctx(finding):
    # suffix after the last ": ..."
    marker = ".statement: "
    idx = finding.find(marker)
    suffix = finding[idx+len(marker):] if idx!=-1 else finding
    # suffix = "..." + repr(ctx)  ; find first quote char
    qpos = min([p for p in (suffix.find("'"), suffix.find('"')) if p!=-1], default=-1)
    if qpos == -1: return None
    try:
        ctx = ast.literal_eval(suffix[qpos:])
    except Exception:
        return None
    return ctx
```
Note repr may use either quote style depending on content; literal_eval handles it.

